1
00:00:04,710 --> 00:00:08,580
No wonder the Ruins of the King's Tomb
have never been conquered.

2
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:14,600
I wasn't expecting to encounter these here.

3
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,880
Denken, can we deal with that, too?

4
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:37,540
The one thing I can say
is that if this weren't a test,

5
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:40,450
I would've shattered my bottle
a long time ago.

6
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:07,040
<i>You're there like the wind</i>

7
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:11,670
<i>Closing your eyes at sunset</i>

8
00:01:11,670 --> 00:01:17,300
<i>I wonder what's on your mind</i>

9
00:01:22,010 --> 00:01:26,020
<i>With your eyelids open</i>

10
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:30,610
<i>Your eyes shone like glass</i>

11
00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:37,360
<i>It faintly smelled like a sunny day</i>

12
00:01:43,290 --> 00:01:48,500
<i>Clear up the sky, let flowers bloom</i>

13
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:52,710
<i>Bloom and blame it on the sunny sky</i>

14
00:01:52,710 --> 00:01:57,090
<i>Even the rain, when it stops</i>

15
00:01:57,090 --> 00:02:02,100
<i>Will make you shine in the sunlight</i>

16
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:07,480
<i>Calm the stirring sounds in my heart</i>

17
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:11,520
<i>We go like the sunny wind</i>

18
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:15,940
<i>Go on and fly over that cloud</i>

19
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:20,780
<i>Further and further away</i>

20
00:02:27,850 --> 00:02:34,710
We call the lord of the dungeon
"Spiegel the Water-Mirror Fiend."

21
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:41,570
It is a monster from a mythical era that
appears in Ewig the Sage's heroic tales.

22
00:02:43,610 --> 00:02:48,750
We believe the Spiegel reads the memories
of those who enter the dungeon

23
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:52,810
and creates perfect replicas of its targets.

24
00:02:54,730 --> 00:03:00,310
There are similar monsters in the
modern era such as the Einsam,

25
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:06,230
but the Spiegel's perfect replicas
have physical substance

26
00:03:06,230 --> 00:03:09,650
and copy the target's
abilities, mana, and skills.

27
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:15,420
It is the reason the Ruins of the King's Tomb
remain unconquered to this day.

28
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:19,290
Why did Sense choose
this dungeon for her test?

29
00:03:19,290 --> 00:03:22,820
A person is evenly matched
against their copy.

30
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:25,570
Defeating them without suffering casualties

31
00:03:25,570 --> 00:03:29,140
requires cool-headed
self-analysis and teamwork.

32
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:37,560
It's exactly the kind of test a pacifist
like her would put together.

33
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:47,410
This isn't good.

34
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,410
We should retreat.

35
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,400
Denken!

36
00:04:01,010 --> 00:04:05,280
Now then, what are we going to do about this?

37
00:04:13,010 --> 00:04:15,240
It's a dead end.

38
00:04:15,530 --> 00:04:17,610
We're cornered.

39
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:35,170
Four-eyes, could I get your opinion
as a cloning magic specialist?

40
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:39,740
I told you, my name is Land.

41
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:42,420
But ask away.

42
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:51,810
How perfect a copy of me
do you think that replica is?

43
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:58,420
Übel, you're chatty even
during combat, aren't you?

44
00:04:59,870 --> 00:05:02,140
It's like you'd die if you stopped talking.

45
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:05,600
You've been watching me closely.

46
00:05:06,350 --> 00:05:09,000
Yeah, that's true. I'd probably die.

47
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:14,530
And yet it's so quiet.

48
00:05:16,730 --> 00:05:20,730
Does that mean it hasn't copied
my memories or personality?

49
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:24,970
No, it's probably just incapable of speaking.

50
00:05:25,510 --> 00:05:33,600
During the initial attack,
it swiped my escape golem bottle.

51
00:05:38,570 --> 00:05:42,510
I see. That <i>is</i> what I would do.

52
00:05:42,950 --> 00:05:45,450
It knows about us, too.

53
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:53,660
It's not attacking despite cornering us
because it's wary of your Sorganeil.

54
00:05:55,170 --> 00:05:59,250
Either that, or it's enjoying tormenting us.

55
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,010
That's not funny.

56
00:06:05,710 --> 00:06:07,560
You're bleeding a lot.

57
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:12,970
You know, you won't last long like this.

58
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:15,290
You're right.

59
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:18,700
Can I ask you one last question?

60
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:23,200
Are you the real one?

61
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:28,200
Who knows?

62
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,520
Uh-huh.

63
00:06:35,730 --> 00:06:37,700
Use my bottle.

64
00:06:40,070 --> 00:06:43,220
But you need that to survive.

65
00:06:43,660 --> 00:06:46,760
Oh, yeah?

66
00:06:47,830 --> 00:06:51,030
In that case, wait here, four-eyes.

67
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:54,780
I'm going to get your bottle back.

68
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:57,150
Hey, wait—

69
00:07:02,850 --> 00:07:05,940
<i>I expected it to close the gap.</i>

70
00:07:06,550 --> 00:07:11,660
<i>I need to see its entire body
in order to cast Sorganeil.</i>

71
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:18,350
<i>Whoever miscalculates the distance first
will lose this battle.</i>

72
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:27,450
<i>If we're evenly matched,
then who wins will come down to luck.</i>

73
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:33,980
<i>I've always been unlucky,
so I don't like luck-based contests.</i>

74
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:41,010
<i>So I have no desire to fight myself.</i>

75
00:07:41,780 --> 00:07:45,560
You must really want to die.

76
00:07:55,140 --> 00:07:57,530
<i>My luck always sucks.</i>

77
00:07:57,530 --> 00:07:59,250
<i>That's why I didn't want to do this.</i>

78
00:08:01,970 --> 00:08:02,620
But...

79
00:08:03,850 --> 00:08:07,370
It looks like your luck was worse.

80
00:08:08,310 --> 00:08:11,500
You were quicker than I expected, four-eyes.

81
00:08:21,830 --> 00:08:26,080
Huh. So the bottle was fake, too.

82
00:08:35,110 --> 00:08:40,000
Übel, you knew that it was a clone
of me that was dying.

83
00:08:40,410 --> 00:08:42,820
Why did you rush to your death?

84
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:46,650
Because I knew you'd come for me.

85
00:08:47,730 --> 00:08:50,710
Do I seem that kind to you?

86
00:08:51,070 --> 00:08:56,130
No, not at all. Not that it matters.

87
00:08:57,370 --> 00:09:02,270
You didn't accept my bottle.

88
00:09:05,830 --> 00:09:09,190
You don't want anyone to die
because of you, right?

89
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:15,500
So I created a situation where
my death would be your fault.

90
00:09:17,810 --> 00:09:20,320
Thanks, four-eyes.

91
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:23,330
I think I learned something else about you.

92
00:09:23,930 --> 00:09:26,740
I see. Good for you.

93
00:09:26,970 --> 00:09:29,180
Are you able to empathize with me yet?

94
00:09:30,350 --> 00:09:32,810
It'll take a little longer.

95
00:09:38,190 --> 00:09:42,280
I think we're pretty close to the bottom.

96
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:47,140
Ms. Frieren, there are stairs over there.

97
00:09:50,260 --> 00:09:53,530
Fern, let me see the map.

98
00:09:55,430 --> 00:09:58,730
I believe we've fully explored this floor.

99
00:10:10,450 --> 00:10:13,490
There's a hidden room behind this wall.

100
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:16,220
There's probably treasure there.

101
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:23,940
I've got a feeling there's a
rare grimoire hidden inside.

102
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:28,980
But we didn't come across anything
that looked like an entrance.

103
00:10:29,750 --> 00:10:31,240
You're right.

104
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:39,430
But based on the structure,
I'm certain there's a room here.

105
00:11:31,810 --> 00:11:34,840
Ms. Frieren, this is incredible.

106
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:46,230
It depicts the achievements
of the king buried here.

107
00:11:47,870 --> 00:11:53,020
I've never seen such a well-preserved
mural of the Unified Dynasty era.

108
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:55,770
This is a valuable discovery.

109
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:01,380
It's magnificent.

110
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:19,520
Our progress has been unnaturally smooth.

111
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:23,030
Are we really going to pass
without incident?

112
00:12:23,590 --> 00:12:25,310
Maybe.

113
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:33,620
What are you all doing here?

114
00:12:34,780 --> 00:12:39,970
Structurally speaking, the bottom of this
labyrinth should be beyond this hall.

115
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:41,730
And?

116
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:46,030
It's been half a day since that
thing took up position there.

117
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:56,500
Huh. This is getting interesting.

118
00:12:56,990 --> 00:12:59,890
Now this is how conquering
a dungeon should be.

119
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:07,130
A perfect replica, huh?

120
00:13:08,010 --> 00:13:12,510
That thing does seem to match my strength.

121
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:18,110
We can't reach the bottom without
doing something about that replica.

122
00:13:18,610 --> 00:13:20,690
Any ideas?

123
00:13:21,220 --> 00:13:28,020
Well, if that's a perfect recreation
of me, then its weaknesses

124
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:31,190
should be the same as the
flesh-and-blood version.

125
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:37,960
Either restraint magic or hypnosis magic
are best for defeating a stronger mage.

126
00:13:38,430 --> 00:13:41,080
I'm resistant to both, though.

127
00:13:41,450 --> 00:13:44,790
But it may create a slight opening.

128
00:13:45,210 --> 00:13:49,590
That would be enough for you to defeat it.

129
00:13:50,530 --> 00:13:51,720
Methode.

130
00:13:52,310 --> 00:13:55,020
You're good at that kind of thing.

131
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:58,010
I wouldn't say I'm good at it, exactly.

132
00:14:00,350 --> 00:14:02,130
Excuse me.

133
00:14:09,110 --> 00:14:11,500
This is interesting.

134
00:14:11,850 --> 00:14:14,430
You're immune to restraint magic.

135
00:14:14,430 --> 00:14:15,560
Smells nice.

136
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:19,490
Normally it should work,
barring a large difference in mana.

137
00:14:20,570 --> 00:14:24,990
Next, Ms. Frieren, could you
please look into my eyes?

138
00:14:28,970 --> 00:14:31,930
Hypnosis magic won't work either.

139
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:37,010
I cannot penetrate
Ms. Frieren's mental defenses.

140
00:14:37,650 --> 00:14:38,910
Oh, my.

141
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:42,640
You really are resistant to both.

142
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:47,740
However, while the construction of your
mental defenses is complex and solid,

143
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:50,530
it seems to be a rather old spell.

144
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:55,830
A specialist in hypnosis magic
may be able to exploit its vulnerabilities.

145
00:14:55,830 --> 00:14:58,560
Do you know any among the test-takers?

146
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:06,130
Edel the second-class mage
may be able to do it.

147
00:15:06,130 --> 00:15:10,730
But unlike me, she has no combat abilities.

148
00:15:10,730 --> 00:15:13,900
Honestly, I'm not sure she'd
be able to make it this far.

149
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:22,210
Also, hypnosis magic only works
on targets that have minds.

150
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:27,210
It's unclear if the replicas
have recreated those.

151
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:32,130
We lack too much information.

152
00:15:35,150 --> 00:15:38,160
Edel, what do you think that is?

153
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:45,340
Who knows?

154
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:52,190
But it's safe to assume it has all the
abilities of the first-class mage Sense.

155
00:15:52,850 --> 00:15:56,440
Concealing our mana and hiding
can only get us so far.

156
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:58,050
We'll have to defeat it.

157
00:15:58,580 --> 00:16:01,170
Do you think we can, Blei?

158
00:16:01,170 --> 00:16:06,850
You and Dünste can't fight properly in
this dungeon, to say nothing of myself.

159
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:12,110
Modern magic isn't suited
to dungeon combat, anyway.

160
00:16:12,810 --> 00:16:15,840
An unwelcome side effect of most dungeons
having already been cleared

161
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:18,190
during the era leading up to
the Demon King's defeat.

162
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:24,070
On top of that, powerful defensive
spells take up too many resources,

163
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:29,220
so most attack spells use natural objects.

164
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:36,510
Manipulating and transforming
objects already in the area

165
00:16:36,510 --> 00:16:41,050
consumes less mana than
creating objects out of nothing.

166
00:16:41,390 --> 00:16:45,810
But that thing does it fairly well.

167
00:16:46,430 --> 00:16:50,430
There are layers of magic cast on its hair.

168
00:16:50,870 --> 00:16:56,240
It probably has numerous methods
it could use to fight inside this dungeon.

169
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:02,960
As I see it, we can't beat that thing.

170
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:06,010
Magic is a world of visual imagination.

171
00:17:06,490 --> 00:17:13,960
To be able to manipulate the uncountably
large number of threads we call hair,

172
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:18,690
it must possess a superhuman imagination,

173
00:17:18,690 --> 00:17:22,430
making it a far greater mage than any of us.

174
00:17:23,310 --> 00:17:27,350
Honestly, it's a miracle we managed
to evade it for this long.

175
00:17:29,010 --> 00:17:31,040
We did our best.

176
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:36,920
But we're not fighters.
It's time for us to give up.

177
00:17:38,630 --> 00:17:42,110
Honestly, I'm scared and want to go home.

178
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:46,820
Edel, does your voice not work on it?

179
00:17:47,220 --> 00:17:51,460
Hypnosis magic is indeed my family's calling,

180
00:17:51,460 --> 00:17:56,580
but it's impossible to meet the conditions
needed to give it sophisticated commands.

181
00:17:57,280 --> 00:18:02,340
At most, I could create an opening
by making it kneel.

182
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:06,140
Even then, I'd have to make eye contact
with it and speak to it.

183
00:18:06,900 --> 00:18:09,090
So it's not impossible.

184
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:12,350
Assuming it has a mind.

185
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:14,970
How much time do you need?

186
00:18:15,330 --> 00:18:19,860
Fifteen seconds. Or rather,
I doubt we'll get more.

187
00:18:20,750 --> 00:18:22,380
What do you mean?

188
00:18:27,350 --> 00:18:28,780
You'll see.

189
00:18:42,510 --> 00:18:44,900
Activate your defensive magic
with full coverage.

190
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:45,660
What?

191
00:18:46,790 --> 00:18:51,780
In modern magic, there are two ways
to defeat defensive magic.

192
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:56,980
Hit it hard enough,
or skillfully slip through it.

193
00:18:58,020 --> 00:19:01,160
Most who use a high number
of attacks are the latter.

194
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,650
I'm surprised.

195
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:07,420
I wasn't expecting both.

196
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:09,890
They have the weight of a boulder.

197
00:19:12,060 --> 00:19:16,930
I thought we'd be able to maintain our
defenses at full coverage for fifteen seconds,

198
00:19:17,350 --> 00:19:20,590
not that it would break through
even before that.

199
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:24,480
But we made eye contact.

200
00:19:25,210 --> 00:19:28,910
The better the mage, the more
closely they watch their opponent.

201
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,220
Kneel!

202
00:19:38,540 --> 00:19:42,020
I see. I understand now.

203
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:44,180
It has no mind.

204
00:19:45,030 --> 00:19:49,300
It's just precisely mimicking
the functions of one.

205
00:19:50,100 --> 00:19:53,420
We can't beat it.

206
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:58,600
You'll have to borrow
the strength of another.

207
00:19:58,600 --> 00:20:02,050
Run as quickly as you can to the fighters.

208
00:20:02,050 --> 00:20:05,060
But as I said, it's time for me
to give up. I'm leaving.

209
00:20:05,450 --> 00:20:07,770
I'm not interested in getting hurt again.

210
00:20:12,790 --> 00:20:16,950
How convenient. It even ensures my safety.

211
00:20:21,010 --> 00:20:22,550
We should run, too.

212
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:29,660
Is there anyone who can
safely reach the bottom?

213
00:20:29,660 --> 00:20:31,060
I told you.

214
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:35,510
She never intended for anyone
to pass from the start.

215
00:20:52,410 --> 00:20:55,330
Currently, we lack information.

216
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:58,820
We should assume it doesn't have a mind.

217
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:02,300
That does mean we'll probably
have to use brute force, though.

218
00:21:03,450 --> 00:21:05,090
Can you do it?

219
00:21:05,090 --> 00:21:06,940
I don't know.

220
00:21:23,970 --> 00:21:28,300
It's impossible to tell what
those things are thinking.

221
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:41,930
<i>But like I thought, it's not a bad matchup.</i>

222
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:54,030
<i>Ehre crushes me or Scharf
in a simple clash of mana.</i>

223
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:09,810
<i>But I know how to win.</i>

224
00:22:18,620 --> 00:22:24,170
No matter the opponent or situation.

225
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:29,590
Brute force, huh?

226
00:22:31,930 --> 00:22:34,250
In that case,

227
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:40,040
I may be able to kill Ms. Frieren.

228
00:22:41,850 --> 00:22:42,770
Oh?

229
00:22:43,390 --> 00:22:44,220
Yes.

230
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,300
Well, then...

231
00:22:47,020 --> 00:22:48,990
Let's come up with a strategy.

232
00:22:50,050 --> 00:22:53,180
<i>And I'm alright</i>

233
00:22:53,180 --> 00:22:56,100
<i>Yeah, I hear you</i>

234
00:22:56,100 --> 00:23:01,690
<i>The wind teases this hair that's longer now</i>

235
00:23:01,690 --> 00:23:04,110
<i>There's meaning in everything</i>

236
00:23:04,610 --> 00:23:07,110
<i>Even the days that came to a halt</i>

237
00:23:07,700 --> 00:23:13,740
<i>Now that I finally understand,
I've caught up to you</i>

238
00:23:13,740 --> 00:23:17,540
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

239
00:23:17,540 --> 00:23:20,420
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

240
00:23:20,420 --> 00:23:25,090
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

241
00:23:25,090 --> 00:23:31,340
<i>I won't ask to see you, so at least</i>

242
00:23:31,340 --> 00:23:37,100
<i>Let me remember the past, just for today</i>

243
00:23:37,100 --> 00:23:43,110
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

244
00:23:43,110 --> 00:23:48,990
<i>No more hesitations, I'd choose the present</i>

245
00:23:50,070 --> 00:23:53,030
<i>Anytime, anywhere, yah</i>

246
00:23:53,030 --> 00:23:57,660
<i>Anytime, anywhere</i>

247
00:23:57,660 --> 00:24:00,660
<i>I'll be there (close your eyes,
and I'll always be there)</i>

248
00:24:00,660 --> 00:24:03,420
<i>Even if there are no absolutes</i>

249
00:24:03,420 --> 00:24:06,460
<i>I'm always aware of your thoughts</i>

250
00:24:06,460 --> 00:24:12,510
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

251
00:24:12,970 --> 00:24:19,430
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby
for you to come back home</i>

252
00:24:20,220 --> 00:24:21,900
That's most of it.

253
00:24:20,810 --> 00:24:22,200
Let's come up with a strategy.

254
00:24:21,850 --> 00:24:23,900
So you had information.

255
00:24:22,700 --> 00:24:24,380
Why don't we work together?

256
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:25,590
Don't you think you should apologize?

257
00:24:24,250 --> 00:24:25,940
I don't like this.

258
00:24:24,670 --> 00:24:26,770
They don't have any weaknesses.

259
00:24:25,870 --> 00:24:27,730
You seem to be enjoying yourself.

260
00:24:27,730 --> 00:24:30,080
It's Frieren's fatal vulnerability.
